CI run 30635617132 (push 6695474), workflow ci, job rust, step
"Clippy (warnings are errors)":

  Checking reproit-backend v0.0.0 (sdk/reproit-backend-rs)
  error[E0433]: cannot find `instrument` in `reproit_backend`
    --> sdk/reproit-backend-rs/tests/behavior_vectors.rs:23:26

Not a lint. The behavior vectors assert the exchange bound and the
divergence marker, which live in the instrument module. That module is
feature gated so the core adapter stays dependency light, so the test file
did not compile under the default features CI's clippy uses.

The local gate that missed it was mine: I ran clippy on two packages
(-p reproit -p reproit-protocol) while CI runs the whole workspace with
all targets, so the SDK crate was never compiled locally at all.

Affected and fixed, measured with the narrow command:

  parent  cargo clippy -p reproit-backend --all-targets   exit 101, 3x E0433
  fix     cargo clippy -p reproit-backend --all-targets   exit 0

Why this is declared an exception rather than no-repro: the gate proves a
no-repro test by overlaying that test file onto the parent commit. Here the
test file IS the artifact being fixed, so the overlay makes the parent
compile and the affected run exits 0 instead of 101. The gate cannot
express a defect whose reproduction is the test file itself. Measured:

  check-fix-policy.py --base 6695474 --head <fix>
  self-dogfood fix policy: affected no-repro test exited 0, expected 101
